  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 101 AM MDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nWill keep this long term discussion short a sweet as there is not \nmuch to talk about with the synoptic set-up that will take hold over \nthe region. Starting off the long term period, Tuesday marks a day \nthat we get a shot of cooler air as an upper-level trough digs \nsouth. This will allow a surge of cooler air to infiltrate the CWA, \nresulting in highs only topping out in the mid to upper 70s. A nice \nbreak from the relentless heat that we have been experiencing. But, \ndon't get to excited with a cooler day and if it will continue, this \nis short-lived as we begin to heat right back up mid-week as ridging \nbegins to build back into the region. As ridging takes a hold, we \nwill remain dry with heat building into Thursday as highs will top \nout in 90s east of the I-25 corridor and mid to upper 80s to the \nwest. The trend heading into next weekend continues as the ridge \nbecomes well established, we look to remain dry and hot. Possibly \nbreaking more temperature records, so stay tuned...",
